  "solution": {
    "brief": "Surface created from curves",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Can be integrated into complex parametric recipes with 80+ components for comprehensive surface generation workflows.\n\nRelated insight: Mid-complexity example: 28-component recipes like '11-3' represent intermediate complexity between basic parametric workflows and complex 80+ component systems.\n\nRelated insight: Updated complexity progression: 15 parameters → 19 components (S11E05) → 28 components (11-3) → 59+ components, showing refined granularity in parametric surface generation scaling.\n\nRelated insight: Recipe 19-04 provides a 45-component example, refining the complexity progression: 28 components (11-3) → 45 components (19-04) → 59+ components → 80+ components, showing more granular scaling in parametric surface workflows.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '3-1' demonstrates 71-component trigonometric parametric workflows, providing a specific data point in the high-complexity range between 59-component (S11E04) and 80+ component systems.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Recipe '3-3' demonstrates 62-component parametric workflows, filling the gap between 59 components (S11E04) and 71 components (3-1) in the complexity progression, representing mid-complexity 3-series recipes.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Unit-02-Class (467 components) provides an extreme upper bound reference point, demonstrating that trigonometric parametric workflows can scale from basic implementations (15-28 components) through high-complexity (71-86 components) to ultra-scale systems (467+ components).",
